00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:03.820
Once you have entered the information
into Excel, it is then time to apply

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:06.990
some formatting to enhance the meaning
and appearance so that it looks

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:10.560
professional and it displays the
information clearly to an audience.

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:13.530
So as you can see at the
moment it's all quite simple.

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:16.200
It's just simply text, there's no spacing.

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:20.010
There is no formatting being
applied, no colours, no borders,

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.600
no shading, anything like that.

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:24.540
So what we're going to do is I'm
going to demonstrate how you can apply

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:27.240
some formatting to this information.

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:32.354
Now, Excel is very similar to
Word and PowerPoint in that it

00:00:32.354 --> 00:00:33.644
has obviously the font group.

00:00:34.065 --> 00:00:36.705
There's a slight difference that it
has what's called the alignment group.

00:00:36.705 --> 00:00:40.605
And this is how you can
align your text in the cells.

00:00:41.114 --> 00:00:44.205
And also you can have the
option to merge cells and center

00:00:44.205 --> 00:00:46.245
cells, and also a wrap text.

00:00:46.515 --> 00:00:50.835
So I'll have a look at some of these
in here, and you can also apply styles

00:00:50.835 --> 00:00:53.265
and format the information as a table.

00:00:54.135 --> 00:00:57.525
So the first thing I want to do is
I need to space this information out

00:00:57.555 --> 00:01:01.875
because it does seem all compressed and
it isn't as clear as I would like it.

00:01:02.475 --> 00:01:06.585
So, what I'll do is I'm going to
widen the rows and the columns, just

00:01:06.585 --> 00:01:07.935
so that the information is clear.

00:01:08.595 --> 00:01:13.215
So if I want to widen them all evenly,
I can click on the little triangle

00:01:13.385 --> 00:01:15.855
in the top corner and select that.

00:01:16.215 --> 00:01:18.585
And as you can see, it's
selected all of the worksheet.

00:01:18.914 --> 00:01:24.414
So if I know click in-between rows one and
two, and then hold the mouse button down

00:01:24.435 --> 00:01:30.720
and just drag it down, it automatically
widens all of those rows evenly.

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:34.560
And again, I can do that with the columns.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:37.770
If I click between B and C, if
I widen them to that, it will

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:41.880
automatically widen the columns evenly.

00:01:42.509 --> 00:01:45.390
So now that I have all the
information there, as you can see,

00:01:45.419 --> 00:01:51.000
the information in column A is being
cut off and there's two options here.

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:54.499
I can widen that one and it
will automatically widen those.

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:59.070
So rather than do that, I just
want to widen that column on its

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:02.370
own, so I click away and then I
can just widen that  individually.

00:02:02.429 --> 00:02:06.300
It doesn't widen the other columns
anymore, that only occurs if you select

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:09.900
everything and then you start widening
it will automatically apply that to

00:02:09.990 --> 00:02:15.510
all the rows or columns, depending
on what you're changing the size of.

00:02:16.829 --> 00:02:18.120
So now I'm happy with that.

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:23.990
As you can see, the text is aligned
to the top on row one, and it is

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:27.920
aligned to the text - is aligned
to the top everywhere, basically.

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:30.360
Now I want to center align everything.

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:35.910
And what actually, what I'll do is I will
bottom align the text in the top row.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:37.830
So that's now at the top.

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:42.420
And if I go up to the alignment and
I'm going to select bottom, so that

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:50.180
aligns it to the bottom and everything
else, I'm going to align to the center.

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:57.480
So that's all now showing clearly so it's
directly central within each of the cells.

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:03.840
So it may be a case that I want to
reduce the width of that column there.

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:07.470
So this will be relevant
to the wrapping text.

00:03:07.769 --> 00:03:13.350
So if I select that column and select
wrap text, nothing happens initially.

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:18.360
But if I reduce the size of that column,
it will automatically wrap the text.

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:23.145
And if I undo the wrap text, as you
can see the information, I would have

00:03:23.145 --> 00:03:28.035
to widen the column again so I can
apply wrap text or take that off.

00:03:28.035 --> 00:03:31.415
And if I don't have it on, I
need to widen that column so

00:03:31.415 --> 00:03:33.525
all the information is clear.

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:37.830
In addition to that, I can
apply the standard formatting.

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:41.130
So for this top row here,
I'm going to make it bold.

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:45.690
And all of the information in column
